WEBVTT

00:02.280 --> 00:05.100
Humanity has been fighting...

00:05.890 --> 00:09.780
with enemies from far away called Festums.

00:47.900 --> 00:50.500
Our choices were to destroy or be destroyed.

00:50.500 --> 00:55.200
Neither side even thought of compromising with the other.

01:43.290 --> 01:45.710
In order for one to live on,

01:45.710 --> 01:47.500
someone had to be the victim.

01:53.060 --> 02:00.300
This is another story of the lives
changed by this never-ending battle.

01:57.800 --> 02:07.000
Soukyuu no Fafner

02:28.280 --> 02:29.920
All right, it's ready.

02:39.680 --> 02:41.550
May I please buy one?

02:42.320 --> 02:43.510
July 20th.

02:43.510 --> 02:47.560
Congratulations on your graduating

02:44.340 --> 02:47.560
It was the second graduation ceremony for this year.

02:48.660 --> 02:55.400
Though it is sad that we are all parting ways on this day,

02:55.400 --> 02:59.200
we will never forget any of you.

03:01.280 --> 03:06.580
I wish you all the best of luck. Please do not forget the time that you've spent on this island.

03:06.580 --> 03:10.130
We hope from the depths of our hearts,
that you all have healthy and prosperous lives.

03:10.130 --> 03:11.810
And with that being said, let us part.

03:15.800 --> 03:19.170
Congratulations on your graduation.

03:23.260 --> 03:24.640
Ryou.

03:25.210 --> 03:27.900
That farewell speech sounded similar to what a student president would've given.

03:27.900 --> 03:28.910
Sure did, didn't it?

03:28.910 --> 03:31.170
I had the vice president help write the speech.

03:31.170 --> 03:33.310
That's what I figured. You lazy bum.

03:34.180 --> 03:36.110
This will be the last time I'll be seeing you too.

03:37.500 --> 03:39.160
You'll be coming back occasionally, right?

03:39.160 --> 03:40.030
Who knows.

03:40.960 --> 03:45.470
Ever since my graduation date was set,
I always felt uneasy about staying on this island.

03:45.470 --> 03:48.890
It'll be easier on me if I just join in with the adults one step ahead of everyone.

03:48.890 --> 03:50.040
I see.

03:50.390 --> 03:53.760
Make sure to be honest about your feelings...

03:53.760 --> 03:56.300
while you're still in school here.

03:56.300 --> 03:58.000
What kind of feelings are you talking about?

03:58.000 --> 04:01.550
Like making a confession to somebody
you like or anything you want.

04:02.010 --> 04:04.800
Regretting is the worst, probably.

04:05.140 --> 04:08.510
You don't have any regrets?

04:08.990 --> 04:11.270
No, I don't.

04:13.630 --> 04:14.520
I see.

04:15.250 --> 04:16.900
Well... later, Ryou.

04:18.650 --> 04:20.040
Goodbye!

04:19.220 --> 04:21.610
To enter a completely different lifestyle...

04:20.040 --> 04:21.610
Let's meet again!

04:21.610 --> 04:24.610
by the time one finishes school.

04:25.200 --> 04:28.580
That was a scene that could only
be seen at Tatsumiya Island.

04:33.450 --> 04:35.620
He's going to lose again.

04:35.620 --> 04:36.670
Lose what?

04:37.110 --> 04:39.710
The usual fight between Kazuki and Kenji.

04:39.710 --> 04:41.880
My bet is on Kenji.

04:42.610 --> 04:44.330
Soushi, who do you want to bet on?

04:44.330 --> 04:47.100
On the other hand,
Kenji has lost the last 13 times.

04:48.070 --> 04:49.640
I'm not interested.

04:50.340 --> 04:51.800
Please excuse me.

04:57.330 --> 05:00.100
They were good friends back then.

05:01.030 --> 05:04.990
Kazuki and Soushi. They used to play together all the time when they were little, remember?

05:06.180 --> 05:10.160
There must be a good reason why
they can't play together anymore.

05:12.160 --> 05:14.170
Hey, Yumi.

05:14.170 --> 05:18.010
I have a favor to ask you,
since you're the vice president.

05:18.010 --> 05:19.380
What is it?

05:19.380 --> 05:20.630
After I graduate,

05:22.430 --> 05:24.590
can you keep him for me?

05:24.590 --> 05:27.560
Idiot! Why don't you take him with you?!

05:27.560 --> 05:28.470
How poor of him.

05:28.470 --> 05:30.470
Ah, you think so, too?

05:31.720 --> 05:34.550
Well then, I have some things to take care of.

05:34.550 --> 05:36.690
Wait a minute, Ryou.

05:36.690 --> 05:38.840
Hi, Masaoka-senpai.

05:38.840 --> 05:40.410
Hey Kuramae,

05:40.410 --> 05:41.590
please take care of the rest.

05:43.880 --> 05:46.610
What's Masaoka-senpai thinking?
Going home already...

05:46.610 --> 05:50.420
Does he know that tomorrow's the closing ceremony?

05:50.420 --> 05:53.790
He didn't want to say that he was going to the hospital.

05:53.790 --> 05:57.620
Just coming here today must have been hard on him.

05:59.500 --> 06:03.800
But, it's a fact that he's lazy.

06:03.800 --> 06:06.000
We need to be on top of things.

06:06.000 --> 06:07.490
Yes.

06:16.310 --> 06:17.800
I'm fine.

06:17.800 --> 06:21.000
I just had a light case of anemia.

06:21.000 --> 06:22.190
What's wrong?

06:23.200 --> 06:24.200
Hey.

06:26.130 --> 06:28.570
Unexpectedly, you're an obliging person, aren't you?

06:28.570 --> 06:31.520
It's just because you had this painful look on your face.

06:31.520 --> 06:35.230
You're not going home with everybody else?

06:35.230 --> 06:36.080
Nope.

06:36.860 --> 06:42.180
You can't just wait for someone
like Kenji to charge towards you.

06:42.180 --> 06:45.500
You need to approach people yourself and become friends.

06:46.690 --> 06:50.480
I probably don't have the right to be saying all this, especially since you're helping me.

06:50.480 --> 06:51.760
Maybe.

06:51.760 --> 06:53.270
Ah, you think so, too?

06:53.270 --> 06:55.390
Toomi Clinic

07:00.360 --> 07:02.860
We finally made it.

07:02.860 --> 07:05.570
Ka-Kazuki-kun!

07:06.030 --> 07:06.940
Hazama.

07:09.530 --> 07:10.530
Thanks a lot.

07:11.310 --> 07:13.650
Let's ask Toomi-sensei for a drink.

07:13.650 --> 07:14.610
No thanks.

07:14.610 --> 07:16.790
Umm, I... have to get going.

07:20.700 --> 07:21.330
Well, later.

07:21.760 --> 07:23.290
B-Bye!

07:24.980 --> 07:26.610
You're here for a checkup, too?

07:26.610 --> 07:29.750
I was fine until I was about to go to sleep.

07:29.750 --> 07:31.740
I wasn't able to go to school today, either.

07:31.740 --> 07:34.300
I was always like that in the past, too.

07:35.100 --> 07:37.560
This is genetic, isn't it?

07:38.040 --> 07:43.130
Masaoka-senpai, you had the
same illness as you mother, right?

07:43.130 --> 07:43.810
Yeah.

07:44.320 --> 07:49.780
As I thought... I wonder if I'm related to my mother.

07:49.780 --> 07:50.960
Who knows.

07:50.960 --> 07:53.820
But I envy you, Hazama.

07:55.280 --> 07:59.080
You have a good mother who really cares about you.

08:00.650 --> 08:01.750
Yes.

08:02.480 --> 08:07.000
Your symptoms have been stable recently, so I'm going to reduce the dosage of your painkillers.

08:07.000 --> 08:10.970
That means that there's no chance of curing it, right?

08:10.970 --> 08:14.470
There's still a chance that the
symptoms might completely disappear.

08:15.260 --> 08:17.630
About that selection I was speaking of before...

08:17.630 --> 08:21.100
Ryou-kun, you don't have to be pessimistic about it at all.

08:21.100 --> 08:25.560
No, that's not it. I'm relieved that
I'm allowed to decide for myself.

08:25.560 --> 08:29.150
I was really scared that I was going
to die without doing a single thing.

08:31.540 --> 08:36.450
It's already been two years since
your mother passed away, hasn't it?

08:36.450 --> 08:37.470
Yes.

08:38.200 --> 08:40.650
Isn't it tough to be living on your own?

08:40.650 --> 08:43.960
It's a small island, so there's always
someone that will look out for me.

08:43.960 --> 08:47.540
And it's not like I'm alone, anyway.

08:50.780 --> 08:53.350
Hazama, you're not going back home?

08:53.350 --> 08:55.890
Maya will be coming home soon.

08:55.890 --> 08:57.500
I see.

08:57.500 --> 08:59.900
I'm envious that you still have your close friends.

08:59.900 --> 09:02.600
About half of mine graduated already.

09:02.600 --> 09:05.610
Masaoka-senpai, you're amazing.

09:05.610 --> 09:09.630
You can go to school regularly and on
top of that, you're class president.

09:09.630 --> 09:10.810
You've got it all wrong.

09:10.810 --> 09:14.230
Everybody decided that on their own while I was absent.

09:14.230 --> 09:15.900
Decided it on their own?

09:15.900 --> 09:16.790
That's right.

09:16.790 --> 09:19.560
The minute I got to school, I was given that title.

09:19.560 --> 09:20.370
I was surprised.

09:20.370 --> 09:23.810
Didn't you hate it?

09:23.810 --> 09:25.330
It seems like you were forced into it.

09:26.640 --> 09:29.590
I was really happy that everybody
hadn't forgotten about me.

09:29.970 --> 09:34.010
I want to repay everyone who gave me a place to be.

09:34.010 --> 09:35.380
That's how I felt all this time.

09:36.440 --> 09:37.810
I envy you.

09:37.810 --> 09:41.560
There might not be a place for me when I go to school.

09:44.190 --> 09:44.800
Look.

09:48.640 --> 09:52.530
You need to cherish your friends who'll stay by your side.

10:01.110 --> 10:02.180
I'm home.

10:05.000 --> 10:07.820
Oh, it's the Principal and Mr. Makabe.

10:07.820 --> 10:09.920
Welcome home, Ikoma-kun.

10:09.920 --> 10:11.270
Please excuse us.

10:11.270 --> 10:13.210
I'll make some tea right now.

10:13.210 --> 10:14.270
No, it's fine.

10:14.270 --> 10:16.050
We just came for a visit.

10:16.410 --> 10:18.050
Well then, Ikoma.

10:18.740 --> 10:20.220
Take care of yourself.

10:25.100 --> 10:29.230
Father. There was another
graduation ceremony this morning.

10:29.980 --> 10:30.940
Is that so?

10:31.770 --> 10:33.400
Isn't it weird?

10:33.400 --> 10:37.910
Having several graduation ceremonies
before summer break even starts.

10:37.910 --> 10:38.740
Is that so.

10:39.600 --> 10:42.000
Maybe it's because it's an island with nothing to offer.

10:42.000 --> 10:45.840
Were the graduation ceremonies
just like this when you were young?

10:45.840 --> 10:46.500
Yeah.

10:47.580 --> 10:51.000
I wonder where I'll go once I graduate.

10:54.550 --> 10:57.800
I'll stay by your side, Father...

10:59.220 --> 11:00.750
In Mother's place.

11:00.750 --> 11:04.950
I won't go anywhere.

11:06.090 --> 11:08.510
Solomon is responding repeatedly.

11:08.510 --> 11:12.070
We shall come in contact with the
response in approximately 700 hours.

11:12.770 --> 11:15.610
This isn't a good time to be intercepting the enemy.

11:15.610 --> 11:19.510
If the Core comes in contact with the enemy while it's forming its own individuality,

11:19.510 --> 11:21.990
there's a high possibility that the
enemy will seize the whole island.

11:21.990 --> 11:26.120
So, are we going to limit the
function of the defense system?

11:26.120 --> 11:29.500
Today, we personally had a talk with Ikoma.

11:29.500 --> 11:33.660
To be precise, all weapons in relation to Fafners are to be locked securely.

11:33.660 --> 11:37.250
To keep the damage we receive to a minimum when the enemy does seize the Fafners,

11:37.250 --> 11:39.010
we have no choice but to seal it ourselves.

11:39.010 --> 11:42.130
But still, it cannot be said that the necessary precautions have been taken with just that.

11:42.130 --> 11:44.850
So, it has been suggested by Ikoma.

11:44.850 --> 11:47.490
Here's the program to avoid the crisis.

11:48.430 --> 11:49.480
Plan L?

11:49.480 --> 11:53.500
The TSXs are necessary to carry this out.

11:53.500 --> 11:55.690
It can't be! Are you suggesting that
the children participate in this?!

11:57.900 --> 12:02.690
We need approval from everyone that manages this island.

12:03.360 --> 12:04.320
Summer break

12:25.190 --> 12:26.520
Kazuki!

12:26.520 --> 12:28.670
I will definitely beat you today!

12:28.670 --> 12:29.520
So don't even think about running!

12:31.720 --> 12:32.350
All right.

12:35.380 --> 12:38.650
You've joined the student council, haven't you?

12:38.650 --> 12:40.920
Yes, I have.

12:40.920 --> 12:43.200
Didn't you think it's going to be a tough job?

12:43.670 --> 12:49.300
The president told me that he comes to school only to play with his dog, not to do his work.

12:49.300 --> 12:53.120
Yeah... I thought it would be fun.

12:54.800 --> 12:59.300
Vice president's job? Or the president?

12:59.710 --> 13:02.260
I'm not sure... Both, I guess.

13:08.350 --> 13:10.410
How are you feeling?

13:10.410 --> 13:11.350
I'm fine.

13:11.350 --> 13:13.560
Umm, Father...

13:14.380 --> 13:18.060
I'm going to go out with my friend for a bit tomorrow.

13:18.060 --> 13:19.020
Is that so.

13:19.020 --> 13:22.230
I was invited by my friend to go to the beach tomorrow.

13:22.650 --> 13:24.200
I'll come home early, okay?

13:43.950 --> 13:47.000
I just remembered how we never had a problem finding a place to play when we were young,

13:47.000 --> 13:49.680
even though we're on a small island like this.

13:54.200 --> 13:56.700
You're not going to swim when
you're the one who invited me?

13:56.700 --> 14:00.000
After seeing your swimming, I lost my confidence.

14:09.020 --> 14:12.730
You've been going to Toomi-sensei's place a lot, haven't you?

14:12.730 --> 14:13.580
Yeah.

14:14.860 --> 14:15.960
How's your health?

14:15.960 --> 14:17.410
It's nothing, really.

14:17.410 --> 14:19.130
It's just a bit inconvenient at times.

14:21.220 --> 14:25.770
I think I can understand the pain
of what those people go through.

14:25.770 --> 14:30.830
I've always been living with my father
so I'm used to taking care of him.

14:32.940 --> 14:35.430
Now that my body's warmed up,
I guess I'll go for a swim.

14:35.430 --> 14:36.650
Are you sure it's okay?

14:36.650 --> 14:38.520
I'm fine. I'm fine.

14:38.520 --> 14:39.330
But!

14:41.230 --> 14:45.180
I never thought I needed taking care of.

14:47.440 --> 14:48.170
I'm sorry.

14:48.730 --> 14:50.820
I'm sorry if I hurt your feelings.

14:55.000 --> 14:58.620
Today was fun, for a change.

14:59.110 --> 15:01.750
It was so fun that...

15:01.750 --> 15:03.210
I was able to forget about my father for once.

15:25.110 --> 15:26.150
Father!

15:27.490 --> 15:28.280
Where are you?!

15:30.820 --> 15:31.860
Father!

15:32.310 --> 15:33.930
Father!

15:33.930 --> 15:34.830
Why?

15:38.980 --> 15:39.870
Father.

15:42.030 --> 15:43.160
What is it?

15:43.160 --> 15:45.000
What do you want to tell me?

15:45.000 --> 15:47.260
I need to...

15:47.260 --> 15:49.380
go to Alvis.

15:49.380 --> 15:51.260
To Alvis...

15:54.660 --> 15:55.500
Father?

15:56.150 --> 15:58.370
Hey, Father?

15:58.370 --> 15:59.750
Father!

16:06.910 --> 16:07.570
Yumi.

16:10.820 --> 16:11.820
Soushi-kun.

16:12.450 --> 16:16.760
Your father often came to visit my father.

16:16.760 --> 16:20.250
Yes. I was told that he was given work-related advice by your father.

16:20.250 --> 16:22.410
Do you know what Alvis is?

16:24.240 --> 16:24.870
No.

16:25.880 --> 16:26.440
I see.

16:44.660 --> 16:45.570
That's Father's...

16:49.570 --> 16:51.780
Plan... L?

16:52.530 --> 16:54.000
Plan L.

16:55.520 --> 16:57.090
Fafner.

16:57.090 --> 16:59.220
Titan model.

17:04.080 --> 17:05.310
Alvis!

17:08.230 --> 17:12.190
It's a card key used to enter Alvis.

17:13.030 --> 17:14.380
Father's voice?

17:14.380 --> 17:17.430
Make your way to Alvis.

17:14.380 --> 17:18.010
What is this? Are you there... father?

17:18.010 --> 17:20.300
Head for the L boat's hangar.

17:18.010 --> 17:20.300
What? What are you saying?

17:22.850 --> 17:23.750
What?

17:33.230 --> 17:34.190
Alvis.

17:35.830 --> 17:36.740
Entrance.

17:43.330 --> 17:45.690
Recognition of level 3 restriction code confirmed.

18:04.740 --> 18:06.270
I know this place...

18:06.700 --> 18:07.500
Why?

18:21.910 --> 18:23.490
What is...

18:25.410 --> 18:26.410
this?

18:32.300 --> 18:33.610
They're Fafners.

18:34.210 --> 18:35.300
Ryou!

18:35.800 --> 18:37.800
Why are you guys here?

18:37.800 --> 18:39.260
TSX.

18:39.820 --> 18:42.370
TSX?

18:44.610 --> 18:46.020
Fafner!

18:46.820 --> 18:49.000
Fafner Titan model.

18:49.770 --> 18:52.100
Our only hope.

18:55.550 --> 18:57.940
Congratulations on your graduation, Yumi.

19:00.850 --> 19:02.830
I'm completely lost.

19:02.830 --> 19:05.820
Father's voice has been resonating
inside my head this whole time.

19:05.820 --> 19:09.810
Information that you memorized
becomes recognized as a voice.

19:09.810 --> 19:11.870
In my case, it was my mother.

19:11.870 --> 19:13.490
Memorized?

19:13.490 --> 19:17.740
Various information that had been implanted subliminally when we were very young.

19:17.740 --> 19:21.520
The world's current condition,
the existence of Alvis within the island,

19:21.520 --> 19:23.720
and a way to fight against the enemy.

19:24.390 --> 19:25.230
The enemy?

19:27.430 --> 19:32.440
So, the ones who find out about Alvis have been graduating?

19:32.440 --> 19:36.430
Once they find out about it,
they can't return to their normal life.

19:36.430 --> 19:39.700
That's why they chose to fight along with the adults.

19:40.480 --> 19:44.090
Why didn't you choose to leave the island?

19:44.090 --> 19:45.160
I've been waiting...

19:45.810 --> 19:50.790
for the execution of Plan L that your father formulated in order to save the island.

19:51.620 --> 19:53.790
I didn't know about it.

19:54.930 --> 19:57.630
About my father also... Nothing at all.

19:59.430 --> 20:04.200
I think my father called me to Alvis because he wanted me to participate in that plan.

20:04.200 --> 20:06.660
That's not it. You don't have a clue about anything at all yet.

20:06.660 --> 20:08.830
And you're saying that you knew about all this all along?!

20:13.570 --> 20:14.700
I'm going home.

20:15.640 --> 20:16.940
I'll take you there.

20:16.940 --> 20:17.800
No thanks.

20:18.710 --> 20:20.280
I don't want to be with you.

20:20.280 --> 20:20.990
Yumi.

20:21.960 --> 20:26.490
There's a part of me that believes if I hadn't gone out with you,

20:27.260 --> 20:30.500
my father wouldn't have ended up like that.

20:32.570 --> 20:33.710
I see.

20:37.060 --> 20:39.960
Toomi Clinic

20:38.280 --> 20:39.960
Masaoka-senpai...

20:40.250 --> 20:41.040
Hey.

20:41.800 --> 20:44.180
Good morning, Puku.

20:45.590 --> 20:48.180
I've desided to graduate.

20:49.470 --> 20:51.850
When?

20:51.850 --> 20:56.160
After summer break is over,
I'm going to leave the island to work with adults.

20:56.160 --> 20:59.720
As I thought, you're amazing, Masaoka-senpai.

20:59.720 --> 21:01.360
I can't work yet.

21:03.030 --> 21:06.360
If I'm able to do it, then so will you.

21:08.420 --> 21:11.410
After I'm gone, please remember that.

21:15.470 --> 21:18.630
Are you willing to set foot on
the same path your father took?

21:19.650 --> 21:20.590
Please let me.

21:29.100 --> 21:30.580
Here is your access card.

21:31.640 --> 21:34.030
Are you going no matter what?

21:34.030 --> 21:35.140
Yes.

21:35.630 --> 21:40.150
I can finally repay everyone who
gave me a place where I belonged.

21:50.120 --> 21:52.870
Since my graduation's decided,
I thought I should at least say goodbye.

21:53.630 --> 21:55.540
I'm going to graduate as well.

21:56.050 --> 21:58.210
In order to participate in my father's plan.

21:58.660 --> 21:59.540
What?!

22:00.020 --> 22:02.340
I went to talk with the Principal earlier.

22:02.340 --> 22:05.500
Idiot! You'll have to fight the enemy now!

22:05.500 --> 22:10.360
So what? Similar plans have been
carried out many times before!

22:10.360 --> 22:12.790
And nobody's ever returned!

22:12.790 --> 22:13.380
Today...

22:13.380 --> 22:15.040
Then why are you participating?

22:19.750 --> 22:21.380
Tell me...

22:21.380 --> 22:23.950
Why did you invite me to the ocean?

22:23.950 --> 22:24.950
I...

22:24.950 --> 22:26.740
You planned to just disappear without a word, didn't you?!

22:29.010 --> 22:30.470
Please, leave.

22:30.470 --> 22:31.970
And stay away from me.

22:41.700 --> 22:44.550
And so, the selected members were gathered.

22:45.120 --> 22:46.890
The best-suited individuals who had undergone...

22:46.890 --> 22:49.550
subconscious memorization with a high Synergetic Code ratio.

22:54.050 --> 22:54.640
Yumi!

22:58.580 --> 23:02.510
My name is Hino Megumi, and I'll be in charge of your training starting today.

23:02.510 --> 23:06.650
If anyone wishes to cancel their participation from the plan, they may tell me at any time.

23:07.250 --> 23:08.400
Understood?

23:09.920 --> 23:12.900
Well then, let me explain the details of Plan L.

23:14.640 --> 23:16.000
Here's a full view of Alvis.

23:16.000 --> 23:19.610
Currently, the enemy is in the midst of searching for this island's existence.

23:19.610 --> 23:21.890
And the main purpose of Plan L is to prevent that.

23:21.890 --> 23:25.510
This letter L signifies the L block of Alvis' left wing.

23:25.510 --> 23:29.150
We will detach this from the island,
and use it as an L boat.

23:29.150 --> 23:32.810
The L boat will continue to travel along the depths of the sea outside of the enemy's detection range,

23:32.810 --> 23:34.960
and will surface once it's out of the island's defense range.

23:34.960 --> 23:38.440
As it attracts the enemies, it will continue to travel along an established route.

23:39.520 --> 23:41.180
The duration is two months.

23:41.180 --> 23:43.880
Our objective is to make the enemies believe that the L boat is Tatsumiya Island

23:43.880 --> 23:46.160
and continue to take the enemies down.

23:46.160 --> 23:48.270
This L boat will be on autopilot.

23:48.850 --> 23:52.030
We will never know our current location.

23:53.140 --> 23:54.600
It will be a rigorous fight.

23:55.190 --> 23:58.040
Exit the room if any of you want to cancel your participation.

24:00.730 --> 24:03.040
Well then, we'll immediately begin the training.

24:05.420 --> 24:09.800
The Fafner's first characteristic is
that there's no need for you to pilot it.

24:10.430 --> 24:13.800
Just obey the information that you have memorized, unify with the Fafner,

24:13.800 --> 24:16.500
and accept the transition in the mind.

24:21.510 --> 24:25.220
This is virtual reality used for training.
Please move as freely as you wish.

24:25.220 --> 24:27.070
Woah. This is...

24:30.570 --> 24:33.590
So this is... a Fafner.

24:36.430 --> 24:37.330
This is great!

24:38.240 --> 24:40.410
I'm able to run!

24:40.410 --> 24:42.030
This fast!

24:42.030 --> 24:44.290
I'm not running out of breath at all!

24:46.670 --> 24:48.230
What is this?

24:48.230 --> 24:50.540
This isn't myself at all!

24:50.540 --> 24:51.500
Father!

24:52.040 --> 24:56.470
The second characteristic is the crossing enabled through the use of a system implemented in each unit.

24:56.470 --> 24:59.760
With this, you'll be able to share your thoughts with each other and prevent the enemy from reading them.

24:59.760 --> 25:01.270
Please accept your partner.

25:01.270 --> 25:02.890
A partner?

25:04.510 --> 25:06.110
Ryou? How?

25:07.190 --> 25:08.300
It must be the crossing.

25:08.860 --> 25:11.870
I object! Please change my partner!

25:11.870 --> 25:13.770
This was done to maintain a balance.

25:13.770 --> 25:16.990
You will soon understand why he's your partner.

25:16.990 --> 25:18.500
What do you mean by understand?

25:20.020 --> 25:21.020
What's this feeling?

25:21.020 --> 25:23.510
Yumi, are you afraid?

25:23.510 --> 25:25.900
Are these Ryou's senses?

25:26.750 --> 25:28.500
Are you enjoying this?

25:29.430 --> 25:31.380
With this, even I can swim!

25:33.590 --> 25:35.140
That's the end of your time limit.

25:35.140 --> 25:36.590
Please step out of the cockpit.

25:37.940 --> 25:43.200
Fafner's third characteristic is the pilot's risk of going through an assimilation phenomenon.

25:43.200 --> 25:45.730
The more and more you pilot it, the more signs of abnormality will appear in your body.

25:45.730 --> 25:49.500
In the worst case scenario, it'll cost you your life.

25:55.750 --> 25:58.290
Go cancel your participation, Yumi.

25:59.480 --> 26:00.800
You're not suited for it.

26:01.470 --> 26:05.120
I will definitely make the plan a success for my father.

26:05.950 --> 26:10.540
Why doesn't a person like you, who has no belief in a safe return to begin with, cancel his participation?!

26:13.440 --> 26:17.600
There were total of eight selected members,
and none of them canceled their participation.

26:18.320 --> 26:20.090
There were four Fafner units in all.

26:20.090 --> 26:22.470
One unit was shared between two pilots.

26:23.220 --> 26:26.280
The max time limit for each battle was set to fifteen minutes per unit.

26:26.280 --> 26:29.270
With two pilots being shifted in and out,
each pilot fought for a total of 450 seconds.

26:30.010 --> 26:33.530
The repetitious combat training.
And then the recognition of the enemy.

26:33.530 --> 26:38.700
Silicon-based life forms called Festums; they are our enemies.

26:38.700 --> 26:42.240
They have a collective consciousness and are suited for various environments,

26:42.240 --> 26:44.820
though none have been found in the ocean as of yet.

26:44.820 --> 26:46.820
The speculation behind it is...

26:46.820 --> 26:50.540
that they assimilate the crystals found in the sea and form into a disorderly mass.

26:51.250 --> 26:54.100
Those were the preparations for our graduation.

26:54.550 --> 26:59.050
There was also another important thing I had to take care of.

26:59.050 --> 27:00.140
Here, Puku.

27:00.140 --> 27:01.420
It tastes good.

27:01.420 --> 27:04.940
He doesn't eat anything besides what I feed him.

27:04.940 --> 27:08.770
He must be able to tell that he's going to be left behind.

27:13.190 --> 27:15.400
It wasn't possible for me to bring a dog along.

27:16.190 --> 27:19.030
As his owner, I was told to take responsibility.

27:23.380 --> 27:28.700
A long time ago, my mother brought him home saying he would be my new friend.

27:29.710 --> 27:34.000
Even on the days I couldn't go to school,
I wasn't lonely as long as I was with him.

27:39.460 --> 27:40.280
No you can't!

27:46.060 --> 27:49.300
You were about to eat it knowing what it was, weren't you?!

27:53.400 --> 27:54.500
Idiot...

27:57.240 --> 27:59.650
Thank you, I'll come again.

28:03.000 --> 28:04.210
Good boy.

28:04.210 --> 28:06.720
You're obediently waiting for Senpai, aren't you?

28:07.470 --> 28:12.170
As a reward, I'll give you a small share of their snacks.

28:12.600 --> 28:15.380
We're in the middle of Nothung model's testing right now.

28:15.380 --> 28:17.490
So it's the rumored new Fafner model, huh?

28:17.490 --> 28:18.380
Yes.

28:18.380 --> 28:21.610
We will do our best to have it prepared by the end of the plan in two months.

28:21.610 --> 28:25.140
That means if we're still alive,
you'll come pick us up, right?

28:26.230 --> 28:27.390
Most certainly.

28:28.720 --> 28:32.350
Masaoka-senpai, it seems like he's hungry.

28:33.930 --> 28:35.060
He's eating it!

28:35.810 --> 28:39.560
Oh, and these are his personal belongings.
It might be a little heavy.

28:39.560 --> 28:42.910
Oh, I'm fine. Thank you for your concern.

28:42.910 --> 28:45.590
Please take good care of him.

28:45.590 --> 28:49.220
Yes. I will take care of him as if it's you.

28:49.220 --> 28:52.620
Umm, it's nothing.
I'll get along with him. Isn't that right?

28:53.060 --> 28:56.330
And right when the last of my preparations were complete,

28:56.330 --> 28:59.400
I began to remember Yumi's words for some odd reason.

29:00.500 --> 29:02.630
"Why doesn't a person like you,

29:02.630 --> 29:05.090
who has no belief in a safe return to begin with,
cancel his participation."

29:05.090 --> 29:06.600
That's what Yumi told me.

29:07.270 --> 29:10.600
Yumi was probably the one who was correct.

29:10.600 --> 29:11.950
And that's what I believed.

29:12.890 --> 29:15.070
Camouflage mirrors, sustained in roaming mode.

29:15.070 --> 29:18.190
Close all dividing compartments in the linked sectors in emergency mode.

29:18.920 --> 29:21.900
Closure of all dividing compartments confirmed.
Opening flooding bays.

29:21.900 --> 29:24.760
Flooding in the linked sectors confirmed.

29:24.760 --> 29:28.820
L boat bridge to CDC,
no abnormalities in the link program.

29:28.820 --> 29:29.990
Flooding complete.

29:29.990 --> 29:31.740
L boat, preparations for launch complete.

29:31.740 --> 29:35.080
Preparations to detach L block are complete.

29:36.640 --> 29:37.630
Detach it!

29:41.050 --> 29:43.800
L boat initiated operation off of the control program.

29:43.800 --> 29:45.500
Heading outside of the Welle Shield's range.

29:46.810 --> 29:48.590
We'll meet them again in two months from now.

29:50.580 --> 29:52.560
Let's pray for their fortune.

29:52.940 --> 29:55.670
Time schedule activated. Operation commenced.

29:56.270 --> 29:58.990
Time schedule activated. Operation commenced.

29:57.050 --> 29:57.940
What's that?

29:59.720 --> 30:02.510
The duration until the plan is completed.

30:03.480 --> 30:07.120
September 2nd, Plan L has commenced.

30:07.120 --> 30:09.390
L stands for left, which has left.

30:09.390 --> 30:11.830
In summation, it means that we have departed.

30:12.520 --> 30:16.300
Just as those words say,
we parted our ways from the island.

30:18.200 --> 30:21.830
Three days after our departure,
our island surfaced.

30:22.880 --> 30:25.500
From today on, this is Tatsumiya Island.

30:28.300 --> 30:30.120
The enemy has materialized.

30:30.120 --> 30:31.350
It's a Sphinx-form.

30:31.350 --> 30:34.310
Divert them with conventional weapons.
Fafners, prepare to sortie.

30:34.310 --> 30:36.640
Power lines 1 to 85,

30:35.060 --> 30:36.640
Siegfried System, link activated.

30:36.640 --> 30:38.970
currently recharging the Fafners through their transfer input ports.

30:38.970 --> 30:39.940
Cockpit block, nominal.

30:39.940 --> 30:41.190
Pilot data, currently being transmitted.

30:41.190 --> 30:42.000
Currently linking.

30:42.000 --> 30:43.310
Releasing all lines.

30:43.310 --> 30:45.170
Green lights confirmed.

30:45.170 --> 30:46.540
Weapon locks, removed.

30:48.790 --> 30:50.580
Nibelung System, code confirmed.

30:50.580 --> 30:52.740
Siegfried System, linkage complete.

30:52.740 --> 30:54.120
Gradual incremental block, in operation.

30:54.120 --> 30:54.660
Hatch opened.

30:55.470 --> 30:57.340
Elevating the movement rails. Linking.

30:58.870 --> 31:00.040
All set!

31:01.060 --> 31:04.780
Input of terrain data, modification data,
and vital data complete.

31:21.320 --> 31:26.750
The first time we saw the enemy,
it was more beautiful than we ever imagined.

31:28.840 --> 31:30.820
Yumi, let's destroy it.

31:52.880 --> 31:54.550
Damn you!

32:24.780 --> 32:27.050
We did it! We defeated the enemy!

32:28.460 --> 32:31.050
Everyone was in good spirits after we had defeated the enemy for the first time.

32:32.140 --> 32:34.550
They were trying to erase their fear with happiness.

32:35.620 --> 32:38.390
It was too late for us to back out of it.

32:39.730 --> 32:43.770
Hey, why did you eat my bread?

32:44.460 --> 32:49.420
I was left in care of others, just like you.
In my case it was Minashiro's family.

32:49.420 --> 32:55.390
Some time ago, there was an incident with a Fafner. There were casualties.

32:56.120 --> 33:00.370
I know. The pilot was killed by the Worm Sphere Phenomenon.

33:00.800 --> 33:03.370
One mistake and you are no more.

33:04.260 --> 33:05.830
Are you still going to do this?

33:06.600 --> 33:14.180
Yes. When I think about Masaoka-senpai,
I'm not afraid of anything anymore.

33:19.950 --> 33:23.470
It's smaller than I thought it would be.

33:23.470 --> 33:26.730
It's because the Siegfried System
isn't implanted in there.

33:27.450 --> 33:28.560
Are you guys ready?

33:28.560 --> 33:29.590
Yes.

33:29.590 --> 33:30.440
Any time.

33:37.970 --> 33:39.950
Mark Ein, stop operation.

33:40.910 --> 33:44.620
As I thought, it's a crucial weakness in unifying with a Fafner.

33:45.630 --> 33:49.330
One more time. Let me try it one more time.

33:55.240 --> 33:56.080
As I thought.

33:56.080 --> 33:56.970
It's not moving!

33:56.970 --> 33:58.650
It's not responding!

33:58.650 --> 34:00.930
The pilot must be unconscious!

34:00.930 --> 34:03.390
Pilot of Unit 3, follow me immediately!

34:03.390 --> 34:03.980
Change of shifts!

34:03.980 --> 34:04.730
Yes, sir!

34:05.190 --> 34:07.390
An enemy came once every two days.

34:19.260 --> 34:22.040
And then somebody vanished.

34:37.670 --> 34:40.550
It happened after our sixth battle.

34:44.290 --> 34:48.600
The more and more one pilots a Fafner,
the more the pilot's body crystalizes.

34:48.600 --> 34:50.560
The assimilation phenomenon.

34:51.630 --> 34:54.820
After our eighth battle, another pilot collapsed.

34:58.550 --> 35:00.200
I was scared...

35:00.200 --> 35:05.000
Not our enemies, but instead, I was scared of the Fafners that were supposedly our weapons.

35:07.810 --> 35:09.610
In order to prevent the exhaustion of the pilots,

35:09.610 --> 35:12.670
I believe that our combat length needs to be shortened from 15 to 10 minutes.

35:13.030 --> 35:15.610
As a result, the number of sorties will increase.

35:15.610 --> 35:19.220
We won't have enough ammunition to divert the enemies at the start of a battle to be doing that.

35:19.220 --> 35:21.790
Conversely, what we should be doing
is increasing the combat duration.

35:21.790 --> 35:23.040
You've got to be kidding!

35:23.040 --> 35:24.290
Ikoma-kun.

35:24.290 --> 35:27.980
Have you been informed of the
details of this plan from your father?

35:28.810 --> 35:29.680
No, sir.

35:30.150 --> 35:34.950
I haven't been informed of the
escape method at the end of the plan.

35:34.950 --> 35:37.800
Even if there isn't an escape method,

35:38.530 --> 35:40.400
I am prepared.

35:41.070 --> 35:42.410
M-My father...

35:43.300 --> 35:45.900
had no intent of sacrificing us all.

35:45.900 --> 35:47.540
Yumi's father wasn't an idiot.

35:48.300 --> 35:50.770
There's no way that he would formulate a plan...

35:50.770 --> 35:52.700
where we would become unable to fight so quickly.

35:52.700 --> 35:54.900
I also believe that we need to shorten
the combat length to 10 minutes...

35:54.900 --> 35:56.960
and prevent the exhaustion of the pilots.

35:56.960 --> 36:01.760
Are you telling me to believe in the planner rather than the situation we're currently in?

36:01.760 --> 36:05.240
Yumi's father was planning to participate in this plan, too.

36:05.240 --> 36:07.220
I think he planned to go back home safely.

36:07.220 --> 36:10.410
So, are you telling me that a person
with an illness in his final hours...

36:10.410 --> 36:12.100
was planning to survive?

36:14.200 --> 36:15.110
Yes, sir.

36:15.110 --> 36:16.940
It wasn't a lie.

36:16.940 --> 36:19.610
Before I knew it, I was also believing in it.

36:20.830 --> 36:22.340
I didn't know the reason.

36:22.340 --> 36:26.420
It's just that I believe that
I would've tried to live harder than before...

36:26.420 --> 36:31.330
if my illness had seriously gotten worse.

36:31.920 --> 36:33.970
Are you on look-out by yourself?

36:33.970 --> 36:35.580
I'm just being lazy.

36:37.460 --> 36:38.170
Are you in pain?

36:38.700 --> 36:39.980
Just a little.

36:39.980 --> 36:42.880
Oh, were you worrying about me?

36:42.880 --> 36:43.960
A little.

36:44.470 --> 36:47.810
Although, I feel that I'll get scolded
by you again if I worry too much.

36:47.810 --> 36:52.530
Back then, I was scared because you brought up my health.

36:53.940 --> 36:55.880
About yesterday, thanks...

36:55.880 --> 36:58.320
for defending my father.

36:58.320 --> 36:59.730
It's not that I was defending him.

37:01.280 --> 37:02.820
More importantly, I'm sorry.

37:04.210 --> 37:05.780
About your father.

37:06.520 --> 37:10.780
I was the one who believed that
I didn't care about returning back alive.

37:12.980 --> 37:15.600
I understood that.

37:16.340 --> 37:19.000
That you always wanted to die.

37:20.080 --> 37:22.800
I felt the same thing in you,
just as I did in my father.

37:23.480 --> 37:26.800
I didn't want you to be like him.

37:33.360 --> 37:36.270
Hey! Come to the lobby now!

37:38.280 --> 37:39.110
This is...

37:39.110 --> 37:42.920
A sector that has been locked all this time has been released automatically.

37:42.920 --> 37:45.060
Those are our supplies.

37:45.060 --> 37:46.240
Why did they do a thing like that?

37:46.240 --> 37:49.060
The enemy has been reading our thoughts,

37:49.060 --> 37:51.860
and attacking according to the amount of weapons we carried.

37:51.860 --> 37:54.530
Deceive your allies before you deceive your enemies, huh?

37:54.530 --> 37:55.450
That's right.

37:55.450 --> 37:58.570
We're given something at a fixed interval.

37:58.570 --> 38:00.210
And in the end, what'll be opened is...

38:00.590 --> 38:02.590
A method to escape.

38:02.590 --> 38:04.470
Yeah. There's no mistake about that.

38:06.220 --> 38:09.220
Your father is as amazing as I thought.

38:09.710 --> 38:12.310
What he wanted was a place to live.

38:12.930 --> 38:15.750
Definitely not a place to die.

38:17.590 --> 38:18.400
Yeah.

38:24.910 --> 38:28.550
I'll select somebody else for the pilot.

38:28.550 --> 38:31.280
I want you to operate the Siegfried System, Soushi.

38:31.280 --> 38:35.620
Are you telling me to send my comrades into the battlefield instead of fighting at the front myself?!

38:35.620 --> 38:37.900
That is your aptitude.

38:40.150 --> 38:44.380
Father, how many people do you think will survive this plan?

38:45.780 --> 38:49.780
The survival rate that Ikoma presented was extremely low.

38:49.780 --> 38:51.890
And yet, you approved his plan?!

38:51.890 --> 38:54.050
And you're telling me to do the same thing as you've done?!

38:54.050 --> 38:55.600
Sacrifice people in order to protect the island?!

38:55.600 --> 38:58.600
Ikoma planned to make it out alive until the end.

38:58.600 --> 39:00.600
That is why I approved it.

39:02.620 --> 39:06.230
I believe in the survival of every one of them.

39:08.370 --> 39:12.200
The will of the people who wish to live no matter how harsh the situation is.

39:13.760 --> 39:17.790
Will I be able to carry this burden, Tsubaki?

39:18.270 --> 39:20.370
Victory

39:18.560 --> 39:20.370
Survival

39:20.370 --> 39:23.130
Our battles continued to increase in their intensity.

39:28.690 --> 39:29.740
Yumi!

39:30.850 --> 39:36.640
An illusion of the seasons that come and go

39:36.640 --> 39:42.720
Reminds me of the memories from my childish days

39:42.720 --> 39:54.000
I thought it was natural to have a place that I could return to

40:01.170 --> 40:07.480
Deep inside my innocent eyes,

40:04.360 --> 40:06.570
Move!

40:07.480 --> 40:13.500
darkness guides the way

40:13.500 --> 40:19.600
Were you born only to suffer?

40:18.060 --> 40:23.140
On that day, one of the four Fafners
that we had became unusable.

40:19.600 --> 40:24.360
Everyone's burdened with a fragment of loneliness

40:25.510 --> 40:27.270
The number of the pilots decreased,

40:25.740 --> 40:32.030
At times, our past is a burden with an importance

40:27.270 --> 40:29.540
and the symptoms of the assimilation
phenomenon in its early stages...

40:29.540 --> 40:32.030
started to appear in the ones who were still able to fight.

40:32.030 --> 40:35.150
Please end already

40:32.030 --> 40:35.890
Hurry!
Hurry! Hurry!

40:32.030 --> 40:35.890
I want to return

40:32.030 --> 40:35.890
Father

40:32.030 --> 40:35.890
We are right here

40:32.030 --> 40:38.000
Although, I won't be able to wish for it more than I can right now

40:32.270 --> 40:35.890
Mother

40:35.910 --> 40:40.330
And finally... some of the pilots started vanishing.

40:38.000 --> 40:43.290
It's impossible to stop...

40:40.670 --> 40:43.290
Hurry, he probably can't get out on his own.

40:44.550 --> 40:49.940
the gears that have begun to move

40:45.540 --> 40:46.490
Yukihiro!

40:50.000 --> 40:56.000
Hesitation... How many times will you attempt to test me?

40:56.000 --> 41:01.720
The distant dream that was shimmering so little

41:01.720 --> 41:08.400
I can fight if there's a place for me to return to

41:03.480 --> 41:06.860
And that was the assimilation phenomenon's final symptom.

41:08.900 --> 41:17.070
I wonder if this muttered voice will reach someone

41:09.840 --> 41:15.030
One by one, our friends started disappearing before our eyes.

41:18.660 --> 41:19.680
We're all
going to disappear
anyway

41:20.140 --> 41:21.120
Idiot!

41:21.120 --> 41:23.570
Why did you write something as stupid as that?! Tell me!

41:23.570 --> 41:24.100
Why did you?!

41:24.100 --> 41:25.080
Please stop!

41:30.840 --> 41:32.230
Please...

41:32.230 --> 41:33.220
stop it already.

41:36.800 --> 41:41.310
Everybody was full of despair, anger, and sorrow.

41:44.740 --> 41:47.600
There were less than two weeks remaining.

41:48.940 --> 41:52.700
And on that day, we lost another Fafner and pilot.

42:01.450 --> 42:03.630
The symptoms of the assimilation
phenomenon in its early stages, huh.

42:03.630 --> 42:04.960
Yes.

42:04.960 --> 42:07.210
Although I'm able to hide it from everybody with this.

42:10.660 --> 42:13.260
I heard that you've successfully operated it for a third time.

42:13.950 --> 42:17.990
Yes, but it's kind of pathetic that the side effects are showing up from just that.

42:17.990 --> 42:21.500
Masaoka-senpai and the others must
be suffering a lot more than I am.

42:22.220 --> 42:24.000
Everybody appears to be peaceful.

42:24.000 --> 42:27.000
So much that I want to let them know the situation that our friends are in.

42:27.000 --> 42:30.400
That would completely nullify what our friends are fighting for.

42:31.120 --> 42:37.530
I wonder if it's right for us to be safe while the others are being sacrificed.

42:37.530 --> 42:40.300
We have no choice but to hope that it's right.

42:42.420 --> 42:45.830
Minashiro-kun, is it true that you finally decided...

42:45.830 --> 42:47.120
to operate the system?

42:48.270 --> 42:49.000
Yeah.

42:50.290 --> 42:53.460
All that remained were two Fafner units,

42:53.460 --> 42:55.740
three pilots,

42:55.740 --> 42:57.300
and the eight adults.

43:04.520 --> 43:05.520
It's an escape sub!

43:05.520 --> 43:07.460
Who would've thought that there would be a passage here.

43:08.020 --> 43:10.040
So this must be the escape method.

43:10.040 --> 43:11.150
Enemy alert!

43:11.150 --> 43:12.290
I'll head out!

43:12.290 --> 43:12.860
Yumi!

43:20.190 --> 43:21.940
Did you see that submarine?

43:21.940 --> 43:23.700
It can hold up to 40 people.

43:24.960 --> 43:28.500
Your father was thinking about everyone's survival.

43:30.060 --> 43:30.710
Ryou.

43:31.570 --> 43:33.580
We made it this far.

43:33.580 --> 43:35.710
We have to make it through, no matter what.

43:35.710 --> 43:38.720
Flood blocks 9 to 17.

43:38.720 --> 43:41.170
Opening dividing compartments 1, 2, and 3.

43:41.170 --> 43:42.880
Escape phase, confirmed.

43:42.880 --> 43:44.720
L boat, Fenrir initiated.

43:45.200 --> 43:48.700
Did they plan to take the Festums down along with this island?!

43:58.090 --> 43:58.650
Yumi!

43:58.650 --> 43:59.560
Ryou!

44:11.870 --> 44:15.380
L boat, 5 seconds left until Fenrir is released.

44:15.790 --> 44:16.380
4.

44:16.770 --> 44:17.380
3.

44:17.380 --> 44:18.380
2.

44:18.380 --> 44:19.150
1.

44:29.230 --> 44:31.400
Responses confirmed within our defense limits.

44:31.400 --> 44:32.870
It's the submarine...

44:32.870 --> 44:33.960
and the Titan models.

44:33.960 --> 44:36.420
Standby for a sortie, Soushi!

44:37.460 --> 44:39.150
Fafner Mark Zwei, launch!

44:44.360 --> 44:47.470
Just wait, I'll bring him back.

44:52.040 --> 44:53.760
Festum at 12 o'clock, right in front of us!

44:53.760 --> 44:56.110
Ready the torpedoes and all missiles!

44:56.110 --> 44:59.090
Enemy also confirmed at Green 25!
No! We're surrounded!

44:59.470 --> 45:00.350
Where are the Fafners?

45:00.350 --> 45:01.500
Approximately 20 kilometers from here.

45:01.500 --> 45:02.700
They won't make it in time!

45:03.400 --> 45:05.680
Since when were they able to go in the sea?

45:07.300 --> 45:08.690
The submarine has sunk!

45:08.690 --> 45:09.700
What did you say?!

45:10.660 --> 45:12.400
The island should be in that direction!

45:12.400 --> 45:12.980
Let's go!

45:12.980 --> 45:14.220
No, you can't, Yumi!

45:14.220 --> 45:15.280
You can't go.

45:15.280 --> 45:19.200
But they already found out that Tatsumiya Island is in that direction!

45:19.200 --> 45:20.690
That's not true.

45:20.690 --> 45:24.620
As long as we aren't 100% sure,
you can't think like that!

45:25.900 --> 45:27.900
We've stayed alive this long, too.

45:29.150 --> 45:31.080
I want to go back.

45:31.080 --> 45:32.580
I want to go back to the island!

45:32.580 --> 45:35.060
Our situation has already changed!

45:35.060 --> 45:38.380
We cannot be the ones who let everyone's efforts go to waste!

45:43.660 --> 45:44.460
Let's go.

45:45.640 --> 45:48.350
Before somebody comes to pick us up.

45:50.420 --> 45:54.480
Senpai, be alive please.

45:54.880 --> 45:56.690
Titan models have started making their move.

45:57.100 --> 45:59.220
They're moving away from the island.

45:59.220 --> 46:01.790
Soushi, stop the Mark Zwei.

46:02.620 --> 46:05.110
There's a possibility that the worst case scenario might have occurred.

46:05.110 --> 46:06.140
But!

46:06.690 --> 46:10.900
We must not endanger the whole island, Soushi.

46:12.630 --> 46:15.370
Mark Zwei, please stop.

46:15.370 --> 46:16.730
What's going on?

46:16.730 --> 46:19.360
Weren't we going to pick them up?

46:19.360 --> 46:21.890
Stay on standby at that spot, Mark Zwei.

46:21.890 --> 46:23.220
The situation has changed.

46:23.220 --> 46:24.490
What the hell is with that?!

46:24.490 --> 46:27.640
We're going to pick them up, aren't we?!

46:27.640 --> 46:29.070
Stay on standby as ordered.

46:29.070 --> 46:31.100
No way! I'm definitely not going to!

46:32.660 --> 46:34.850
Lock the Mark Zwei's controls.

46:38.540 --> 46:40.890
Please let me go, Minashiro-kun!

46:40.890 --> 46:42.110
I'm begging you!

46:42.110 --> 46:46.010
Minashiro-kun! You can hear me, can't you?!
Why aren't you answering me?!

46:46.010 --> 46:48.140
Please, Minashiro-kun, let me go!

46:48.140 --> 46:49.540
Minashiro-kun!

46:51.430 --> 46:56.740
CDC, the ones that are there are units and pilots with actual fighting experience.

46:56.740 --> 47:00.870
If we recover their data,
our strength will improve greatly,

47:01.360 --> 47:03.600
and we can use it to resist against enemy invasions.

47:05.160 --> 47:06.260
Soushi.

47:06.260 --> 47:09.140
Are we going to overlook this great opportunity...

47:09.140 --> 47:11.260
in gaining the strength to be able to defeat our enemy?!

47:11.260 --> 47:12.850
Then what are these Fafners for?!

47:16.590 --> 47:17.620
Go ahead.

47:17.620 --> 47:21.440
Under one condition. I will not allow you to take the Fafner out of our defense limits.

47:22.790 --> 47:24.570
Thank you very much, Father.

47:26.540 --> 47:29.220
Mark Zwei, reorganize the unit.

47:29.220 --> 47:32.080
And... pursue the targets at full speed!

47:32.080 --> 47:32.680
Roger.

47:34.640 --> 47:38.110
Measure all oscillations detected in the area around the targets.

47:38.110 --> 47:38.800
Yes, sir.

47:41.710 --> 47:45.250
Only time will tell us the answer.

47:47.340 --> 47:49.480
Data on the tidal currents has been gathered.

47:49.480 --> 47:53.800
If we're lucky, what's left will reach the island from here.

47:55.430 --> 47:56.830
Ryou...

47:56.830 --> 47:57.350
Yeah?

47:59.270 --> 48:01.810
Thank you for stopping me.

48:06.290 --> 48:08.000
Hey, Yumi.

48:09.430 --> 48:10.400
What is it?

48:15.270 --> 48:16.300
I love you.

48:18.650 --> 48:21.100
No, I've loved you...

48:22.050 --> 48:24.600
probably for a long time now.

48:24.960 --> 48:29.940
I'm not sure if I love you or not.

48:29.940 --> 48:34.600
I went past that part of my life before I was aware of it.

48:36.190 --> 48:37.000
I see.

48:42.290 --> 48:44.660
Everything we did up till today...

48:45.320 --> 48:48.690
will reach everybody on the island, right?

48:49.890 --> 48:50.490
Yeah.

48:53.360 --> 48:55.970
I wonder if Father would have praised me...

49:00.300 --> 49:01.980
Snow?

49:01.980 --> 49:03.330
In the depths of the ocean?

49:03.810 --> 49:05.200
Marine snow.

49:06.770 --> 49:08.000
Everybody...

49:09.010 --> 49:12.840
Everybody must be praising us.

49:14.820 --> 49:15.760
Ryou...

49:16.530 --> 49:20.500
I'm glad that you're the one who's by my side right now.

49:21.480 --> 49:24.060
That's how I truly feel right now.

49:25.130 --> 49:25.910
I see.

49:28.000 --> 49:31.860
I wonder if this means that I love you...

49:34.490 --> 49:38.330
But I feel something more than that from this.

49:41.580 --> 49:44.200
Because you were by my side,

49:44.760 --> 49:45.640
I was...

50:00.350 --> 50:01.490
Yumi?

50:03.860 --> 50:05.800
Hey... Yumi?

50:09.670 --> 50:12.420
You're not there anymore, are you, Yumi?

50:28.080 --> 50:29.840
And that is all.

50:29.840 --> 50:31.500
That was our fight.

50:32.920 --> 50:37.100
I pray that somebody will hear this someday.

50:48.540 --> 50:51.690
The reason you couldn't go in the ocean was because...

50:51.690 --> 50:55.860
you weren't able to renew yourselves and end up crystalizing.

50:56.650 --> 50:58.580
But renewing yourselves...

50:58.580 --> 51:01.370
means that your body's being born again, right?

51:02.370 --> 51:05.870
And you guys have gained that ability as well.

51:05.870 --> 51:08.100
That also means...

51:08.100 --> 51:09.870
that you also have lives, right?

51:09.870 --> 51:12.040
Fenrir released.

51:20.450 --> 51:22.100
Confirmed the exact location in the abyss.

51:22.100 --> 51:23.500
It is believed...

51:24.330 --> 51:27.010
Fenrir was utilized in the depths of the sea.

51:27.010 --> 51:28.470
There is only one answer.

51:29.890 --> 51:33.500
There was a concern that the units
were to be assimilated by the enemy.

51:34.710 --> 51:41.000
This was a message to us that the Festums were also in the depths of the ocean.

51:43.920 --> 51:46.670
Mark Zwei, return to base.

51:47.540 --> 51:50.960
Nobody is there anymore.

51:59.070 --> 52:05.410
— Four months later —

52:06.110 --> 52:10.310
This was found when it came in contact with the First Welle Shield's tidal current sensor.

52:10.310 --> 52:11.960
With its vital data.

52:11.960 --> 52:13.100
Does that mean that...

52:13.100 --> 52:13.900
Yeah.

52:14.350 --> 52:17.480
The pilot utilized Fenrir after analyzing the currents.

52:18.500 --> 52:21.200
It's proof that the pilot was calm until the end.

52:22.280 --> 52:25.200
I wonder who was piloting it...

52:22.500 --> 52:33.500
How long will it take for our hearts to be connected?

52:25.200 --> 52:27.250
From the investigation,

52:27.250 --> 52:29.690
it seems that there was a voice recording left behind.

52:31.880 --> 52:33.960
Wait a minute! What's wrong Puku?

52:34.900 --> 52:44.500
It would be nice if I'm able to heal a lonely smile

52:36.130 --> 52:37.500
Could it be that...

52:46.480 --> 52:57.500
I was too close to notice the person most dear to me

52:55.430 --> 52:56.380
And that is all.

52:56.830 --> 52:58.360
That was our fight.

52:58.840 --> 53:09.450
I'm able to feel happy just having you by my side

52:59.500 --> 53:03.480
I pray that somebody will hear this someday.

53:09.450 --> 53:15.460
Even on nights of sadness, and on mornings of joy...

53:15.460 --> 53:22.000
you were watching over me

53:23.000 --> 53:33.330
Though my only word of "thanks" could not reach you

53:33.330 --> 53:39.530
I was a little scared to become modest

53:34.340 --> 53:35.260
Puku...

53:38.280 --> 53:43.270
As you've hinted, the one who was in here was Masaoka-senpai.

53:39.530 --> 53:52.000
Now that I'm in your arms, my heart is opening up to you...

53:44.890 --> 53:49.000
He was probably with Yumi-senpai until the end.

53:52.000 --> 54:01.500
while being held in this gentle peace

53:55.900 --> 53:57.000
Good boy.

53:58.000 --> 54:00.320
You went straight to...

54:00.320 --> 54:04.670
Masaoka-senpai's side, didn't you?

54:10.440 --> 54:21.500
Outside the window filled with a sudden silence, show falls and scatters

54:15.500 --> 54:20.340
I'm going to return ahead of everyone.
I want to take him back to Tatsumiya Island.

54:20.340 --> 54:22.870
Solomon is showing signs of a response.

54:22.870 --> 54:25.610
It'll be tough, but it's expected that
we'll be intercepting them at Alvis.

54:22.870 --> 54:33.340
In a world stained in pure white, I'm drawn in closer by your sound

54:25.610 --> 54:29.480
It was only peaceful for half a year.

54:29.480 --> 54:34.620
Does this mean that the battles our friends went through only had a small significance?

54:33.340 --> 54:39.580
I was a little scared to become modest

54:34.620 --> 54:40.020
We are constantly living in a peaceful world that somebody else won for us.

54:39.580 --> 54:52.260
Now that I'm in your arms, my heart is opening up to you...

54:41.830 --> 54:45.630
Even if it were only a day of peace,

54:47.140 --> 54:50.470
I will be grateful for its value.

54:52.260 --> 55:02.000
while being held in this gentle peace

54:52.320 --> 54:53.500
You're right.

54:55.480 --> 54:56.800
I'll be waiting...

54:57.500 --> 54:59.020
for the time when we'll be able to fight together.

55:04.030 --> 55:07.500
That is how peace and war has been passed down.

55:09.000 --> 55:10.610
Their will to live.

55:11.370 --> 55:13.470
The pain of the ones who fight at the front.

55:14.550 --> 55:18.000
Will I be able to carry this burden?

55:19.040 --> 55:22.000
I continued asking that same question to myself over and over.

55:26.050 --> 55:29.640
That answer is somewhere inside the upcoming battles.

55:30.590 --> 55:32.450
Within our battles.
